{"seq":37,"at":"2026-10-23","kind":"created","target":{"type":"fact","id":"f28407"},"reason":"New question added to grow the article from five to six facts: What is the Monday before Ash Wednesday called, the high point of the Rhineland carnival with its great parades in Cologne, Düsseldorf and Mainz? (answer: Rose Monday), verified against the cited sources.","by":"fact-count-rework","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosenmontag"},{"url":"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosenmontagszug"}],"changes":[{"field":"answerEn","new":"Rose Monday"},{"field":"answerDe","new":"Rosenmontag"},{"field":"answerRu","new":"Розовый понедельник"},{"field":"spans","new":{"en":[1575,11],"de":[1651,11],"ru":[1610,19]}},{"field":"timeline","new":{"kind":"event","start":"1823-02-10","end":null,"precision":"day","approx":false,"ongoing":false,"labelEn":"Cologne's first Rose Monday parade","labelDe":"Der erste Kölner Rosenmontagszug","labelRu":"Первое шествие Розового понедельника в Кёльне"}},{"field":"source","new":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosenmontag","title":"Rosenmontag – Wikipedia","lang":"en"}}],"hash":"bf80073fd428"},
